From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:27:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: a terminal's record keeps whom it sent messages to

hc send from inside a terminal adds { to, count, last_ms, text } to the
sender's record (one entry per receiver, the latest last, at most 32; text
is the last message's first line), with a sent event. Receivers on another
machine are kept by this core's name for it, and records mirrored from a
machine read the same way here, so a panel can draw who talks to whom.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
